=== SURVEY ===
Surveyed existing widget patterns:
- WidgetShell: accepts title, icon, loading, freshness props (updatedAt, isFetching, isStale, isError, onRefresh)
- WidgetDetailCard from ./shared: takes DetailEntry[] with label/value/badge/mono, supports compact (slices to 4), handles empty state
- useVehicleSpecs(vehicleId?: string) → VehicleInfoEnvelope<Record<string, unknown>> (staleTime STATIC)
- useVehicleOptions(vehicleId?: string) → VehicleInfoEnvelope<Record<string, unknown>> (staleTime STATIC)
- useVehicleConfigLatest(vehicleId: number, refetchInterval?) → VehicleConfigSnapshot | null
- VehicleConfigSnapshot fields: car_type, trim, exterior_color, wheel_type, version (no aux_battery_type)
- Registry pattern: id, name, description, icon, category, defaultSize, minSize, maxSize, component (lazy)

=== REASONING ===
- Standard (2×4): build DetailEntry[] from specs + config data for model/trim/paint/wheels/interior/auxBattery/carVersion + option badges
- Compact (1×2): centered model + trim text only (no options)
- Three hooks aggregated: specs (string vehicleId), options (string), config (number)
- Freshness props: max of all three dataUpdatedAt, OR-combine isFetching/isStale/isError
- Null safety: asString() helper for unknown → string | null; fallback chains across specs/config
- aux_battery_type not on VehicleConfigSnapshot — sourced from specs only
- configData cast to Record<string, unknown> for CompactView prop compatibility

